  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo></math> where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math> denotes the greatest integer function. Then the number of points of discontinuity of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know that the greatest integer function is discontinuous at integral points.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, are the integer values.</p><p>At&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, which means that function is continuous at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8800;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>Hence, the function is discontinuous at points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>The number of values is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math> .</p>",
    "image": null
  },
